<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: an x86-32 callee's stack purge, proven by its own code
    (kuna_calleepurge, always on).

    Issue:      kuna GH-1554 - x86win.cspec leaves the extrapop of its
                __stdcall/__thiscall/__fastcall models unknown. A call no later
                merge pins gets StackSolver's guess, which for an internal
                callee is "pops nothing", so every stack offset after a
                __stdcall call is shifted by its argument bytes: later calls
                lose stack arguments and the caller's locals alias their
                outgoing-argument slots.
    Stage:      P4 calls - ActionExtraPopSetup (`p4_calls/kuna_calleepurge.rs`).
    P0 assert:  none (a correctness fix).

    stdcallpurge_pe_i386.exe (VC8 /O2, build notes in stdcallpurge_pe_i386.s):
    split (0x401080) calls the five-argument __stdcall dist twice and the
    six-argument __stdcall corte once, each through a `jmp` thunk, and passes
    &os/&ot to corte.

    calleeframes_pe_i386.exe (clean-room asm, notes in calleeframes_pe_i386.asm):
    use_add2 (0x4011b0) calls the __stdcall add2 twice; the second call's third
    argument is read after the first call's pop. map_string (0x401110) calls
    the CRT-shaped alloca_probe_16 -> chkstk helper between two LCMapStringW
    calls and hands the buffer to freea; the helper returns with ESP lowered by
    EAX, so its `ret` states no pop, and every call keeps its arguments.
    seh_open (0x4010b0) is framed by the CRT-shaped seh_prolog4/seh_epilog4,
    which return with the stack pointer moved; its call to add2 keeps both
    arguments it reads through the frame pointer the helper set.

    calleedepth_pe_i386.exe (clean-room asm, notes in calleedepth_pe_i386.asm):
    start (0x4010e0) calls the __stdcall outer, which calls the EBP-framed
    __stdcall framed, which calls wrap, which calls a function framed by the
    CRT-shaped seh_prolog4 on one of its two paths. The walk of outer reaches
    that function with its helper call cut off by the depth limit; wrap, whose
    only imprecision comes from that call, is not taken for a stack-moving
    helper, so framed and outer state their `ret 4` and start's later call
    reads start's own argument.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
