  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/stdcallpurge_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x401080 as split</com>
  <com>load function split</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/calleeframes_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x4011b0 as use_add2</com>
  <com>load function use_add2</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x401110 as map_string</com>
  <com>load function map_string</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x4010b0 as seh_open</com>
  <com>load function seh_open</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/calleedepth_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x4010e0 as start</com>
  <com>load function start</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #1: the first thunked __stdcall call keeps all five arguments" min="1" max="1">v1 = \(float4\)\(float10\)sub_401190\(a0,a1,a2,a3,a4\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #2: the second call is read at the stack depth the first one left" min="1" max="1">= \(float4\)\(float10\)sub_401190\(a1,a2,a3,a4,a0\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #3: the six-argument call gets its arguments and the two local addresses" min="1" max="1">sub_401195\(v1,a4,a0,a1,&amp;v4,&amp;v3\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #4: the locals the callee writes are read back, not split" min="1" max="1">return \(float10\)\(float4\)\(\(float10\)v4 \+ \(float10\)v3\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #5: the frame-pointer __stdcall add2 takes its two arguments" min="1" max="1">= sub_4011a0\(a0,a1\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #6: the second add2 call reads the third argument past the first one's pop" min="1" max="1">sub_4011a0\(a2,v[0-9]+\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #7: both LCMapStringW calls around the alloca helper keep six arguments" min="2" max="2">LCMapStringW\(a0,a1,a2,a3,[^,()]+,[^,()]+\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #8: freea keeps the buffer the alloca helper made room for" min="1" max="1">sub_4010f0\([^()]+\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #9: the call inside the SEH-framed function keeps both arguments" min="1" max="1">= sub_4011a0\(v[0-9]+,v[0-9]+\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPURGE #10: a caller of a stack-moving helper keeps its proven pop at every depth" min="1" max="1">sub_4010d0\(a0\);</stringmatch>
